<urn:usf:acceptance:fixture-process-validation> <urn:usf:predicate:text> "Stage A independently validates mode policy, exact launch construction, authority/currentness and refusals using the previously admitted no-child-process validator. It integrates only the bounded adapter; it does not select the new mode for itself or claim real process conformance. After that integration, a separate semantic selection may admit Stage B fixture process checks. The new mode must allow exact Node/Git/flock fixture processes inside private PID/network namespaces and fixture scratch only; deny undeclared executable inodes including copied scratch executables and direct dynamic-loader invocation, network, ambient secrets and live-host supervisor access. Check and integration must bind the same exact mode, launcher, tools, schemas, command, source closure and time limits and refuse any drift. Missing kernel/host support refuses without weakening the default. Real negative runtime tests remain required before any dependent stewardship acceptance. Preserve bounded anonymous fixture standard-I/O channels without enabling named/abstract connections or inet networking; derive this adapter repair from the actual private-profile getsockname denial, not speculative permission widening." <urn:usf:graph:fixture-process-validation> .
