<urn:usf:requirement:fixture-validation-bootstrap> <urn:usf:predicate:text> "The adapter construction and Stage A validation remain on current proof-warranted work and the previously admitted no-child validator. Meaningful pure policy, argument, currentness and refusal tests run without subprocesses. Stage A may integrate only the bounded adapter and reusable private AppArmor policy asset. It may not prepare or load a host profile. The exact raw source-asset digest and single-profile compiled parser-output digest are independently observed and must refresh construction authority. These parser observations do not establish a loaded policy; selected execution still refuses absent or mismatched kernel evidence. A later operator-authorised host preparation must use those exact current reviewed asset bytes for profile identity usf-fixture-process-v1, only exact STACK-only local include fragments, and bounded target-name, loaded-and-attached readback and rollback evidence. It must never use ux, pux, profile replacement transition, broad change_profile or checker-driven kernel policy auto-load. Only then can a separate explicit Stage B transition select the process mode for real positive and adversarial negative tests; no circular self-validation." <urn:usf:graph:fixture-process-validation> .
