<urn:usf:requirement:fixture-validation-environment> <urn:usf:predicate:text> "Clear ambient environment and credentials; explicitly set contained HOME/USF_PROVIDER_HOME and fixture TMPDIR. Only fixture scratch is writable. The authority copy and dependencies remain read-only; private procfs supports process identity and monotonic time without access to live host PIDs. A selected mode requires exact AppArmor profile identity usf-fixture-process-v1, exact repository asset raw SHA-256 and matching kernel profile raw_sha256 plus enforce mode read from unprivileged `/sys/kernel/security/apparmor/policy/profiles/*/{name,mode,raw_sha256,sha256}`. The checker never reads a hand-authored .usf host receipt as that evidence. Placeholder, mismatch, absence or stale evidence refuses. Preserve current 120s timeout,5s settlement grace and output bound. Refuse missing primitives or unsupported host; never silently run unconstrained. Required process standard I/O is local IPC, not network reachability: permit only anonymous AF_UNIX stream socket-pair creation, getattr, read-only getopt metadata inspection and local shutdown of anonymous streams, plus send/receive to anonymous fixture peers whose validated stack components are usf-fixture-process-v1, bwrap and unpriv_bwrap, and the existing unconfined checker peer on inherited standard descriptors. Keep named/path/abstract socket bind, connect, listen and accept and all inet networking denied. The launcher closes all extra descriptors before verified Node exec. No broad unix/network grant, new host channel, credential access or live supervisor communication follows. Actual selected runtime must prove outer and nested fixture I/O while preserving confinement. Actual follow-up kernel audit denied getsockopt after getattr was admitted. The exact Node v24.16.0 libuv uv_guess_handle source performs getsockname then getsockopt(SOL_SOCKET,SO_TYPE) before recognising AF_UNIX stdio: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/nodejs/node/v24.16.0/deps/uv/src/unix/tty.c . This warrants only anonymous stream socket option reads; setopt and named/network connection permissions remain denied. A later complete read-only audit multicast observation identified the fatal nested stdio operations: socket_shutdown and peer label match failures for bwrap and unpriv_bwrap, separately from twelve nonfatal setopt denials. Exact Node/libuv process.c ignores socket buffer tuning errors; do not grant setopt merely to suppress these logs. Anonymous shutdown and send/receive for each already validated stack component are required for actual nested pipe completion. Source: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/nodejs/node/v24.16.0/deps/uv/src/unix/process.c and https://raw.githubusercontent.com/nodejs/node/v24.16.0/src/spawn_sync.cc ." <urn:usf:graph:fixture-process-validation> .
