<urn:usf:requirement:fixture-validation-exec-confinement> <urn:usf:predicate:text> "Use existing bwrap for private PID/network/user namespaces and read-only declared view. The prior Landlock-only three-inode strategy is refused because it cannot execute dynamic Node while keeping direct loader invocation denied. The replacement adapter must authenticate exact private AppArmor policy asset src/realisation/fixture-process.apparmor, profile identity usf-fixture-process-v1, declared Node/Git/flock bytes and launcher inputs. After bwrap, Python preserves all prior labels, verifies target profile presence and enforce mode via the kernel policy filesystem, and stacks only that target. It never loads kernel policy. Later host preparation may use only exact STACK-only local include fragments and must expose bounded loaded-and-attached readback evidence. ux, pux, profile replacement transition, broad change_profile, execution or executable mapping from writable scratch, copied executable, loader, shell, interpreter, fallback exemption and checker-driven kernel policy auto-load are prohibited. The launcher may use the installed fixed Python3.12 interpreter solely before restriction; child invocation of that interpreter is not allowed. Actual Stage B observation proved that a pathname Unix socket can listen under the file write grant even though anonymous Unix rules do not admit bind. AppArmor pathname sockets use file mediation, so Unix-rule deny or a narrower writable scratch glob cannot distinguish required regular-file writes from socket binding. Complete the existing launcher confinement with a fixed, additive seccomp BPF filter before verified Node exec: deny bind, listen, accept, accept4 and connect with EPERM for every process descendant; leave socketpair and inherited anonymous stdio usable. Deny io_uring_setup, io_uring_enter and io_uring_register as alternate asynchronous socket-operation entry points; installed Linux headers expose IORING_OP_ACCEPT, CONNECT and SOCKET and syscall numbers425/426/427 on both admitted architectures. No inherited io_uring descriptor survives existing descriptor closure. Authenticate supported x86_64/aarch64 architecture in the BPF program and refuse other ABI syscall entry, including x32; retain exact source-bound fixed syscall numbers from installed Linux headers. Require no_new_privs and successful filter installation with filter-mode readback; absent support, failed install/readback or unsupported machine refuses before corpus execution, with no fallback. Do not accept a caller-supplied filter or add host-policy auto-loading. Preserve the existing wire, AppArmor executable/mapping policy, bwrap read-only view, exact tools, scratch, descriptor closure and time limits. Stage A source/policy acceptance does not claim runtime filter effectiveness; separate Stage B must execute the actual positive process/lock/stdio and negative socket/native observations. Kernel primitive source: https://docs.kernel.org/userspace-api/seccomp_filter.html ." <urn:usf:graph:fixture-process-validation> .
